{
 "note": "Cape Leeuwin lighthouse keepers' cottages (1896, George Temple Poole), from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and the inHerit record. Three single-storey stone cottages in a row down the east side of the cape, about 44 m apart, each under one broad pyramid roof of grey corrugated iron (about 17 m square over the verandahs), with a detached stone laundry behind and a round stone tank. The two southern cottages are limestone, the northern one local granite/gneiss. One is a museum. The verandah under the roof edge has no posts here (the spec's verandah is one skillion on the front). Metres: x left (north) to right (south) as seen from the access road on the west, y back (east).",
